title: "Estimated Daily Visitors to Siesta Key Beach"
format: html
execute:
  echo: false
  message: false
  warning: false
---

## An illustrative scatter plot

A local vacation-rental provider reports an estimate of **2.2 million visitors
per year** to Siesta Key Beach, but does not publish daily attendance counts.
The plot below uses simulated visits: each dot represents one visit, and the
annual total is randomly allocated across 2025 days, with weekend days given
slightly higher weight. This weekend effect is an assumption for illustration,
not observed beach data.

```{r}
library(tidyverse)

set.seed(2026)

daily_weights <- tibble(
  day = seq.Date(as.Date("2025-01-01"), by = "day", length.out = 365)
) |>
  mutate(
    weekday = as.integer(format(day, "%u")),
    weight = if_else(weekday >= 6, 1.25, 1)
  )

daily_visits <- as.vector(
  rmultinom(n = 1, size = 2200000, prob = daily_weights$weight)
)

attendee_dots <- tibble(
  day = rep(daily_weights$day, times = daily_visits),
  visit_rank = sequence(daily_visits)
)

ggplot(attendee_dots, aes(x = day, y = visit_rank)) +
  geom_point(color = "#2D7FA3", alpha = 0.35, size = 0.15) +
  scale_x_date(date_breaks = "1 month", date_labels = "%b") +
  scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::label_comma()) +
  labs(
    title = "Simulated beach visits across the year",
    subtitle = "Each dot represents one simulated visit; weekends are weighted 25% higher",
    x = "Day in 2025",
    y = "Visit number within each day",
    caption = "Synthetic allocation of the 2.2 million annual estimate; daily values are not observed counts."
  ) +
  theme_minimal()
```

There are 2.2 million dots, so they overlap at this display size. The source
does not identify unique people or describe its counting method; these dots
represent modeled visits, not actual people or measured daily attendance.

## Source

- [Gulf Coast Vacation Rentals: Siesta Key beach facts](https://www.gcvacationrentals.com/florida%C2%92s-top-rated-beach-siesta-key/) —
  reports 2.2 million annual visitors.

